               tumor progression often involve the accumulation of multiple
               gain-of-function abnormalities in individual cells. The
               co-occurrence of Her-2/neu overexpression and EGF receptor
               overexpression in the same aneuploid cells defines an
               adeno/squamous genetic evolutionary sequence that is common to
               ductal breast cancers, non-small cell lung cancers, and other
               solid tumors. Later steps in this sequence include ras and c-myc
               overexpression. The neuroendocrine genetic evolutionary sequence
